    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d99">

                <pb facs="0417" n="242" xml:id="pg242"/>

                <head>99. Memorandum from McClintock to Rostow, December 15, transmitting a memorandum from Woodward to McGhee and Ramsey, which attaches
                    a memorandum from Woodward to
                        McGhee<anchor n="1" xml:id="d99-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <date ana="#date_undated-inferred-from-document-head" calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1961-12-15">December 15, 1961</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <pb facs="d99-1" n="1" type="facsimile" xml:id="d99-1"/>
                <list subtype="subject" type="description">
                    <label>SUBJECT</label>
                    <item>Ecuador</item>
                </list>
                <p>You will be interested I believe in the first page of Mr. Woodward’s memo on conclusions to be drawn
                    from our experience of the recent revolt in Ecuador. You will note that his
                    third paragraph substantiates the observation made in our paper on Preventive
                    Diplomacy as to the importance of indoctrinating the military in various
                    countries with American ideas of respect for constitutional order.</p>





                <xi:include href="d99-a1.xml" xpointer="d99-a1"/>
                <xi:include href="d99-a2.xml" xpointer="d99-a2"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d99-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d99-f1-content">
                <p>Preliminary analysis of recent Ecuadorian revolution. Secret. 6 pp. WNRC, RG 59, S/P
                    Files: Lot 67 D 548, Ecuador.</p>
